From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] binman: use importlib.resources instead of pkg_resources

binman dies as soon as the SPL is linked:

    tools/binman/binman ... build -u -d u-boot.dtb ...
    File ".../tools/binman/control.py", line 16, in <module>
        import pkg_resources
    ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pkg_resources'

pkg_resources was a setuptools module, deprecated for years and dropped in
setuptools 81; wrynose stages setuptools 82.0.1, so it is simply gone. The
recipe already depends on python3-setuptools-native - there is no longer
anything there to depend on.

control.py already imports importlib.resources and uses it at line 738, so use
it for the two remaining pkg_resources calls as well:

  - resource_string() returns bytes and the caller decodes utf-8 itself, so
    read_bytes() is the match, not read_text().
  - resource_listdir() returns bare filenames, which is what the .py filter
    just below expects, so take .name off each entry.

Both were passed __name__ ('binman.control'); pkg_resources resolves that to
the containing package, so address 'binman' directly, as line 738 already does.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [u-boot 2024.01 is pinned here for RK3566;
fixed upstream in later releases]
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
 tools/binman/control.py | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/tools/binman/control.py
+++ b/tools/binman/control.py
@@ -13,7 +13,6 @@
     # for Python 3.6
     import importlib_resources
 import os
-import pkg_resources
 import re
 
 import sys
@@ -96,7 +95,8 @@
             msg = ''
         return tag, msg
 
-    my_data = pkg_resources.resource_string(__name__, 'missing-blob-help')
+    my_data = (importlib.resources.files('binman')
+               .joinpath('missing-blob-help').read_bytes())
     re_tag = re.compile('^([-a-z0-9]+):$')
     result = {}
     tag = None
@@ -151,7 +151,8 @@
     Returns:
         Set of paths to entry class filenames
     """
-    glob_list = pkg_resources.resource_listdir(__name__, 'etype')
+    glob_list = [item.name for item in
+                 importlib.resources.files('binman').joinpath('etype').iterdir()]
     glob_list = [fname for fname in glob_list if fname.endswith('.py')]
     return set([os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(item))[0]
                 for item in glob_list
